  "customfield_10187": null,
  "description": "<p>When retrieving a FedoraAcl resource, the subjects of the returned triples do not include the \"/fcr:acl\" part of the path.</p>\n\n<p>PUT /foo/fcr:acl</p>\n\n<p>PATCH /foo/fcr:acl<br/>\n INSERT DATA</p>\n\n{ &lt;#authz&gt; a acl:Authorization ; ... }\n\n<p>GET /foo/fcr:acl<br/>\n &lt;/foo#authz&gt; a acl:Authorization ; ...</p>\n\n<p>I would expect the response to the GET request to be:</p>\n\n<p>&lt;/foo/fcr:acl#authz&gt; a acl:Authorization ; ...</p>\n\n<p> </p>\n\n<p>It should also be noted that the non-hash subjects are also incorrect - ie /foo rather than /foo/fcr:acl.</p>",
